<title>NORWAY: Norway's Navia raises stake in UK Whessoe.</title>
<headline>Norway's Navia raises stake in UK Whessoe.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Navia ASA said on Thursday it, together with Swiss group Endress+Hauser, had increased its shareholding in Britain's Whessoe Plc to around 51 percent.</p>
<p>The Norwegian hi-tech group which specialises in marine, airport and offshore instrumentation, said the stock was bought at 175 pence per share. Navia said it held around 34 percent of the shares while Endress had 17 percent.</p>
<p>It said documents bidding for the remaining equity had been circulated to Whessoe's shareholders.</p>
<p>Last Friday Whessoe said it had withdrawn its recommendation of a bid by British engineering giant Siebe Plc and said it would back the rival offer from Navia and Endress+Hauser.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
